The attached image illustrates Nano-11's effectiveness in antigen targeting and retention. Panel a shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) containing OVA express the highest levels of the costimulatory molecule CD86 in draining lymph nodes. Panel b further characterizes OVA-positive MigDCs as predominantly CD11b+Ly6C-, indicating specific cell targeting. Panel c demonstrates in vivo that OVA formulated with Nano-11 (OVA+N11) is retained at the injection site for a significantly longer period (up to Day 7) compared to soluble OVA alone, which clears by Day 2, highlighting Nano-11's role in prolonged antigen availability.